      "level": 2,
      "content": "SECTION A: TIME, SPEED & DISTANCE"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Section A covers fundamental concepts of Time, Speed & Distance, speed conversion, average speed, relative speed, and train problems.",
        "Section B focuses on Basic Mensuration divided into two-dimensional (2D) and three-dimensional (3D) figures.",
        "Section C introduces Basic Data Interpretation techniques commonly required for aptitude tests.",
        "Includes a dedicated Practice Questions section accompanied by a complete Answer Key for practice and verification."
      ],
      "id": "5hkxh1c"
    },
    {
      "id": "9d180l5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "1. BASIC CONCEPT"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wpg2wpl",
      "content": "Speed = Distance / Time<br></br>Distance = Speed × Time<br></br>Time = Distance / Speed<br></br><br></br>SSC questions from this area are direct and calculation-light."
    },
    {
      "id": "ry6212d",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "2. SPEED CONVERSION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "va8c15x",
      "content": "1 km/hr = 5/18 m/s<br></br>1 m/s = 18/5 km/hr<br></br><br></br>Example:<br></br>36 km/hr = 36 × 5/18 = 10 m/s"
    },
    {
      "id": "cr4b5rp",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "3. AVERAGE SPEED"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "d7skg82",
      "content": "For equal distance:<br></br>Average speed = (2xy)/(x+y)<br></br><br></br>Example:<br></br>40 km/hr and 60 km/hr<br></br>Average speed = 48 km/hr"
    },
    {
      "id": "gb70t6w",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "4. RELATIVE SPEED"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gdgbah7",
      "content": "Same direction: Difference of speeds<br></br>Opposite direction: Sum of speeds<br></br><br></br>Example:<br></br>50 km/hr and 70 km/hr (opposite)<br></br>Relative speed = 120 km/hr"
    },
    {
      "id": "7r22cdt",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5. TRAIN PROBLEMS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "z4doxcr",
      "content": "Time to cross an object = Length / Relative speed<br></br><br></br>Example:<br></br>Train length = 100 m, time = 10 s<br></br>Speed = 10 m/s"
    },
    {
      "id": "akeh82p",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "SECTION B: BASIC MENSURATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "69mnsm4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "6. 2D FIGURES"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "z15o6z4",
      "content": "Square:<br></br>Area = a², Perimeter = 4a<br></br><br></br>Rectangle:<br></br>Area = l × b, Perimeter = 2(l+b)<br></br><br></br>Circle:<br></br>Area = πr², Circumference = 2πr"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tq58o16",
      "content": "Example:<br></br>Radius = 7 cm<br></br>Area = 154 cm²"
    },
    {
      "id": "cpdqusw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "7. 3D FIGURES"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "eu8ah3u",
      "content": "Cube:<br></br>Volume = a³, TSA = 6a²<br></br><br></br>Cuboid:<br></br>Volume = l × b × h<br></br><br></br>Cylinder:<br></br>Volume = πr²h"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2sv1231",
      "content": "Example:<br></br>Cube side = 5 cm<br></br>Volume = 125 cm³"
    },
    {
      "id": "nrhogkc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "SECTION C: BASIC DATA INTERPRETATION"
